import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>9.1c — Polymorphic Party: Mixed Character Types</h1>

<div class="callout warn">
    <strong>Season 2: beyond the exam.</strong> This topic is no longer tested
    (the 2025 CED removed inheritance from the exam). We build it after May 12
    because it makes the RPG engine dramatically better, and because you are
    ready for it. Pure craft, zero test anxiety.
</div>



<div class="activity expand-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Expand Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~30 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Build: Party with Polymorphism</h3>
        <p>The real power of inheritance is polymorphism: a Character[] array can hold Warriors, Mages, and any future subclass — and each one behaves according to its own overridden methods.</p>
        <p>Using your Character/Warrior/Mage classes from 9.1b:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Create a <code>Character[] party = new Character[4]</code>.</li>
            <li>Fill it: Warrior("Aldric", 40, 12, 5), Mage("Mira", 25, 8, 50), Warrior("Grom", 50, 15, 7), Mage("Lyra", 20, 6, 40).</li>
            <li>Create an Enemy (just use Character): Character("Dragon", 80, 10).</li>
            <li>Loop through the party: each member attacks the Dragon. Print results.</li>
            <li>The Dragon attacks back — it picks a random party member each round. Use a loop until either the Dragon or the entire party is dead.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Polymorphism in Action</h3>
        <p>When you call <code>party[i].attack(dragon)</code>, Java calls the Mage's attack() for Mages and Warrior's attack() for Warriors — even though the array type is Character[]. This is dynamic dispatch. What would you need to change to add a Rogue class?</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-09/extends-and-super.html">Inheritance</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-09/polymorphism.html">Polymorphism</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
